    "text": "Psychologists are professionals who study human behavior, emotions, and mental processes. They use scientific methods to understand how people think, feel, and interact. Psychologists work in various settings, including hospitals, schools, research labs, and private practices. They may specialize in areas like clinical psychology, counseling, developmental psychology, or forensic psychology. Their work involves assessing individuals, diagnosing mental health conditions, and developing treatment plans. Psychologists also contribute to research and education, helping to improve mental health care and understanding of human behavior. Their role is essential in promoting mental well-being and supporting individuals in overcoming psychological challenges.",
